@startuml
!theme plain
title TASK-260715-30lv40 — M2 capability lifecycle and M3 handoff
hide empty description
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

state Idle
state Connecting {
  [*] --> Base
  Base -right-> RelayBootstrap : base prepared; no routes
  RelayBootstrap -right-> Activation : validated candidate (still inactive)\nor finite unavailable
}
state Full #lightgreen
state Degraded #lightyellow
state "Relay-only reprobe" as Reprobe #lightyellow {
  state "Waiting\n(timer registered)" as Waiting
  state "Running\n(attempt registered)" as Running

  Waiting -down-> Running : current timer / retire timer registration; allocate attempt
  Running -up-> Waiting : eligible failure / retire attempt; register next timer
}
state "Reasserting\n(M3-owned)" as Reasserting #lightblue {
  state "Awaiting current base" as AwaitingBase
  state "Validating relay\n(M2 reconnectValidator registered)" as ValidatingRelay

  [*] --> AwaitingBase
  AwaitingBase -down-> ValidatingRelay : current BaseReady / M3 local validation-start event
}
state Stopping #lightgray
state Failed #pink

[*] -right-> Idle
Idle -right-> Connecting : accepted start / larger runtime generation
Activation -right-> Full : BaseReady && candidate proof /\natomic bind + promote + open UDP
Activation -down-> Degraded : BaseReady + finite unavailable /\nregistration=null
Connecting -down-> Stopping : mandatory failure or stop

Full -right-> Degraded : relay-only loss / retire registration; invalidate UDP
Degraded -up-> Waiting : automatic eligibility or accepted local relay-policy revision
Waiting -down-> Degraded : exhausted or ineligible / retire timer
Running -down-> Degraded : noneligible failure or exhausted / retire attempt
Running -down-> Full : fresh complete validation / promote activeSession

Full -down-> Reasserting : current M3-owned recovery event
Degraded -down-> Reasserting : current M3-owned recovery event
Reprobe -down-> Reasserting : clear registration; cancel and yield
ValidatingRelay -up-> Full : candidate success / atomic T26; clear reasserting
ValidatingRelay -up-> Degraded : finite candidate failure / retire first; atomic T27

Full -down-> Stopping : mandatory base loss or stop
Degraded -down-> Stopping : mandatory base loss or stop
Reprobe -down-> Stopping : clear registration; base loss or stop
Reasserting -right-> Stopping : terminal M3 outcome or stop
Stopping -up-> Idle : confirmed ordinary stop cleanup
Stopping -right-> Failed : failure cleanup or route clear uncertain
Failed -up-> Connecting : explicit start / larger runtime generation

note right of Reprobe
Public service remains degraded: (1,1,0).
Waiting has exactly one current timer registration;
Running has exactly one current attempt registration.
Both are prospective: active relay stays null, UDP closed,
and retired associations invalidated.
Retirement clears each registration before cleanup or reschedule.
end note

note bottom of Degraded
tcp=1, safeDNS=1, udp=0
General UDP rejected; no physical fallback.
Exhaustion re-enters only through accepted local
relay-only policy evidence, never UI or M3.
end note

note top of Full
tcp=1, safeDNS=1, udp=1
Authenticated SSH + packet/TCP + safe DNS
+ current validated live relay.
end note

note right of Reasserting
M3 exclusively owns reconnect and provider reasserting.
After current BaseReady, M3 may start exactly one M2 validator.
activeRelayGeneration stays null and all bits stay false
until T26 or T27 proves and publishes the target state.
end note

note bottom of Failed
tcp=0, safeDNS=0, udp=0
Route state may truthfully remain clearFailed.
No absolute OS kill-switch claim.
end note
@enduml
